; A chirality-verify profile: the sub-category where every morphism is total
; (open-edge 9, docs/totality.md). The (total) clause makes the profile demand
; that every def in the composite is proven total -- structural recursion,
; coverage, and strict positivity all discharged. `chirality verify` reports it.
;
;   python3 -m chirality verify demo/verify-total.chiral
;
; Every def below is total: `sum-to` recurses structurally on the list it folds,
; `main` is non-recursive. A guarded counting loop would prove too (measure-based
; termination); an UNGUARDED one -- (def spin (-> I64 I64) (lam (i) (spin (+ i 1))))
; -- does not, and adding it turns verify INVALID.

(import "ports/ports")

(def sum-to (-> (List I64) I64)
  (lam (xs)
    (case xs
      (nil 0)
      ((cons h t) (+ h (sum-to t))))))

(def main (=> Unit Unit) (lam (u) u))

(target totalizer (require main (=> Unit Unit)))

(profile p (ports halt) (target totalizer) (total))
